WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.303 --> 00:00:03.880
- Can I have your attention please?

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.200
Everyone put your hands
up and no one gets hurt.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.710
Now, one of you will send
me all your users' data

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.410
and credit card information right now.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.370
You, start working
(gun clicks)

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.608
and no one gets hurt.

00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:16.441
- Okay.

00:00:16.441 --> 00:00:18.060
(dramatic music)

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.850
Uh huh, I actually don't know how.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.960
- You do work here, right?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.340
- Yeah, I, I, I do, I do,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.280
but I've never worked
on this codebase before

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.660
'cause it's not my job.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.683
So I don't know.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.473
He does.

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:31.320
(dramatic music)

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.153
- Give me the data.
(gun clicks)

00:00:32.153 --> 00:00:32.986
I'm not playing around.

00:00:32.986 --> 00:00:33.819
- Okay. Okay.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.601
(keyboard clicks)

00:00:42.116 --> 00:00:42.949
(gun clicks)

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:45.060
- Don't tell me you're
trying to call the cops on.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.893
- No, no, no.

00:00:45.893 --> 00:00:47.730
I just need two-factor authentication

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.860
to remotely access our servers.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.263
- You lie to me and I
blow your brains out.

00:00:53.263 --> 00:00:56.846
(dramatic music continues)

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.940
Goddamn, what is taking so long?

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.020
- I'm sorry.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:07.080
Sometimes it takes a
while to receive the text.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.930
Let me try again.

00:01:08.308 --> 00:01:09.396
(phone buzzes)

00:01:09.396 --> 00:01:11.451
Oh, oh, I received both of them.

00:01:11.451 --> 00:01:14.130
(keyboard clicks)

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.120
All right.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:15.993
I sent it.

00:01:17.775 --> 00:01:20.970
(dramatic music continues)

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.820
- I don't see it.

00:01:25.327 --> 00:01:26.160
I'm not fucking around.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.380
Where the fuck is my data?

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.250
- I did send it.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.083
Look.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:31.920
I sent the Slack message
to my manager, okay,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.050
to request read access to the database.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.310
- You don't have read access?

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.960
- Well, I haven't worked on it in a while

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.523
so I lost my privileges.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:39.570
(slack notification)

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.238
Oh, okay, I got it.

00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:43.740
(keyboard clicks)

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.573
Oh, shoot.

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:48.060
I forgot.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:48.900
- What?

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.240
- I'm so sorry, but for me to get it

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.073
I need to

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.473
file a ticket to IT.

00:01:56.353 --> 00:01:57.960
- IT?

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:58.983
Are you kidding me?

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.920
Even I know that'll take weeks.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.300
- I'm so sorry.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.556
Please don't shoot me. I have a family

00:02:05.556 --> 00:02:07.556
- And my equity
hasn't fully vested yet.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:10.620
- All right, fuck it.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.050
Where do you guys store your snacks?

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.202
- At the micro kitchen over there.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.452
(food packages rustle)

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.590
- I'm not gonna leave
this place empty handed.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.720
- Holy shit.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.870
Should I put this on
my performance review?

